to  take out Piccolo the reveal of this  secondary plot thread added further  tension to the event's proceedings but  what it didn't do was Elevate yamcha's  situation making him feel like more of  an afterthought and with strike after  strike blow after blow Yamcha is looking  as though he's going to be knocked out  of bounds by the God of this world who  by the way doesn't seem to have tried  very hard at all viewing Yamcha is  nothing but a stepping stone on his way  to fight Piccolo later and this is where  it gets interesting as I mentioned the  story of this fight is a perfect mirror  image of Piccolo's fight with Krillin  both involve winners that hide their  identities to varying degrees for the  purposes of the tournament both enter  their respective battles anticipating it  to be nothing special but both get  impressed by their respective opponents  abilities with Piccolo taken aback  almost immediately and Kami at the very  end  in devastating fashion  [Music]  I don't know what is much like the prior  fight these Pages demonstrating the  initial strike of yantra's energy ball  and the subsequent counter by Kami  exemplify perfectly what it is about  toriyama's paneling that I adore there's  such a powerful sense of movement the  pages almost feel kinetic filled with  life and flow and in the end revisiting  these quarterfinals I was honestly Blown  Away by the level of quality present  throughout with the surprising level of  thought having gone into the encounters  the themes present and Breakneck action  paneling to rival any of the other  tournament fights that came before it  and with the semi-finals now approaching  I think you can now appreciate why I  think the 23rd Tenkaichi Budokai is a  contender for the very best Arc the  Dragon Ball series has ever produced the  semi-finals  [Music]  Son Goku vs ten shinhan in fittingly  grandiose fashion the finals from the  prior tournament are now acting as the  semi-finals for this tournament the last  time these two faced off it was close  but tensionhan managed to squeak out of  victory in the end to win the 22nd  Tenkaichi budakai so how do things  measure up now well the entire fight  while great at its core is there to show  just how amazing Goku has become and I  think tenshinhan was the perfect  candidate to bring that out of the  character similar to the prior fights  the paneling is Stellar with some really  interesting angles and ideas  experimented with but for me I think the  largest contribution this fight made to  the series was the introduction of  voighted clothing in fights  weighted clothing wasn't necessarily A  New Concept of Dragon Ball at this point  as it had been established during  Roshi's training before the 21st  tankaichi Budokai all those years ago  however as I alluded to earlier never in  this way before this is once again  another concept or idea introduced in  early Dragon Ball that will become  exceptionally popular later in z  and Z used to tremendous effect right  here in this scene to achieve one thing  to place Goku in a position of mystery  and control throughout this tournament  no matter what match was taking place in  the quarterfinals Goku would remark upon  each encounter with tremendous insight  and observation skills lending to the  idea that he is more in control and more  powerful than even we as an audience  might appreciate and that very aspect of  the story being told through this fight  is emphasized through this very action  he's been concealing his power from both  his opponent and us the readers or  viewers tension on remarks beforehand  that he's impressed by Goku's  Improvement but that his speed is still  nothing compared to his own leading him  to outmaneuvering Goku at every turn  however despite this two things remained  consistent Goku never got tired and Goku  never had a problem tracking his  movements and this all starts to make  sense when you realize he wasn't able to  move as fast as he wanted to placing  Goku once again on another level above  everyone else which isn't an unfamiliar  position for him to be in during these  tournaments throughout the 21st and 22nd  Tenkai a key aspect of these tournaments  surrounding Goku has been that of how  competent he actually is and the story  surrounding them have been discussing  how best to overcome the mountain he  presents to the likes of roshi and  others however what makes this Arc  unique when taking that aspect into  account is that unlike the previous arcs  where Goku is the obstacle in this Arc  Goku is the point of view character the  hero we see his internal thoughts as he  tries to piece together what's going on  between Shen and Piccolo and even ten  shinhan and Tau and that's what makes  this Arc so special he's not the  obstacle Piccolo is and right now  tenshinan is blocking the way to Piccolo  and that long sought after a first place  spot strongest under the heavens  needless to say things aren't looking  too good for the crane school alumni but  what I really like about this section is  that ten shinhan doesn't roll over and  take this sudden show of ability by Goku  as an indication that he's lost hell no  he's the defending Champion instead in  response to that he whips at a move no  one has ever seen before including Goku  in the past we've seen after image  techniques and we've even seen grow  extra limbs in the prior about three  years ago but this time he takes that to  its natural conclusion by splitting  himself into four separate but identical  Fighters and the presence of this scene  serves two purposes one to demonstrate  how tenacious gifted and hard-working  tension on is as a fighter and two to  show us all that Goku not only has  developed physically as made obvious  earlier in the fight but that he has  sharpened his mind greatly also  so  I really appreciated the angle this  fight has taken it places Goku once  again in the driver's seat and creates  all of this anticipation with his very  statement alone begging us the readers  to try and figure out what those two  weaknesses might actually be that he's  talking about overall this fight  delivers on just about every front it's  a terrific settling of a score produce  some wonderful paneling and showcase  some clever action writing with the  weaknesses Goku exposes in this  technique not only making sense but  because they made sense it only further  cemented how much more adaptive fighter  Goku has become over the last three  years Goku advances to the finals in  dominating fashion next up  Shen vs Piccolo Jr  with one match between two Rivals now  having reached its conclusion we press  onward to another between Kami  inhabiting the body of a civilian named  Shen versus The Reincarnation of the  Demon King his other half Piccolo Jr and  while it's one of the shortest  semi-final matchups its design is simple  but immensely effective these  semi-finals while interesting in their  own ride with some interesting action  set pieces were designed with the clear  mission of establishing and building up  the contestants of the final match up  above all else with this fight against  Shen used to outstanding effect in  helping to elevate Piccolo higher than  we ever could possibly have foreseen  something you might have noticed during  this review however is that despite  having acknowledged Piccolo as the main  villain of the Ark I've not done much in  the way of speaking about him Beyond his  relationship to Kami and that's with  good reason if you were to go back  through the previous Arc and this one to  compare the two incarnations of their  respective piccolos the king and The  Reincarnation you'd notice that while  sharing some ID theological similarities  they are markedly different Piccolo Jr  throughout these contests seems to have  shown some respect to his fellow  competitors on some level during  numerous fights either while watching or  participating Piccolo acknowledges the  power and toughness of his opponents  going as far as to admit what he's being  proven wrong this isn't something King  Piccolo would ever have done with him at  the first sign of resistance pushing  back or losing his mind to blinding  anger however when Piccolo was taken  aback and shown resistance he applies  strategy and counter measures  foreign  the fight itself is littered with some  interesting back and forth with some  telling pieces of dialogue and actions  taken it's an effective fight lending  opportunity to develop Piccolo raise the  stakes of the event and even at times  elevates Goku in subtle ways during the  Shen vs Piccolo fight on the first page  of chapter 181 after seeing the  Breakneck pace of the opening to this  match everyone is left stunned roshi  Krillin tenshinhan Yamcha everyone  except for Goku without words this helps  him stand out from the crowd ahead of  his match in the finals and on the topic  of the finals match there's a brief but  interesting back and forth between Kami  and Goku right before he goes out to  fight Piccolo in the semi-finals and  within it the pieces are set for Goku to  become the character he will remain for  quite some time into Z and Beyond  throughout this series Goku has been a  character that when faced with  expectation and reality shatters those  expectations innovating new ways around  problems people never thought possible  at present Kami doesn't think Goku has  what it takes to do what he things he  needs to to kill Piccolo Jr and Goku  doesn't want to kill Piccolo knowing it  will in turn kill Kami and there my  friends lies the main problem of this  Arc Piccolo has sealed Kami inside a  vial and swallowed it and now Goku is  the only fighter remaining to protect  the world from the wrath of this  Sinister individual but if the last  number of arcs and indeed these last  couple of fights have taught us anything  about Goku is that when he's backed up  against the corner and given two options  he's the sort of character to grit his  teeth dig deep and create a third to  find another way when no one else could  this is what I call a true heroes moment  and it's all coming to a head for the  finals of the 23rd Tenkaichi Budokai the  finals  Piccolo Jr versus Sun Goku of all the  fights in Dragon Ball none other better  signal the rise of the younger  generation more so than this right here  Goku who surpassed his older master and  Piccolo who's just dominated Kami and it  all comes to a head in the finals of the  best tournament in the series it's  established early on that Goku is  fighting with a self-imposed handicap  well okay actually two not only does he  want to defeat Piccolo but he needs to  protect the spectators surrounding him  and in addition to that he still wants  to win the tournament all this time as  an audience we've been focused on  Piccolo and the threat he presents  overcoming him and freeing Kami but Goku  he just might do it something of note  also during this match is that the  battle contains the inspiration for some  of the most iconic moments and set  pieces from Goku's fight with Vegeta  take for example their beam struggle  during the gorge battle it's iconic but  the exact same scene took place with the  exact same framing in this battle with  Piccolo and if that wasn't enough  remember Goku's battle with uzaru Vegeta  one massive difference between these two  battles with giant opponents is how the  scene serves Goku or depicts him for  lack of a better term in the Vegeta  fight as many of you might remember Goku  is firmly on the back foot which  admittedly has its own benefits in  creating additional tension moving  towards the climax but in this Piccolo  fight the science disparity isn't used  to overwhelm Goku but to instead subvert  the audience and prop Goku up and  demonstrate how tough he is and how  intelligent he can be he openly refuses  any help from anyone else like ten  chinan or Krillin citing it as grounds  for disqualification something he's  actively trying to avoid while trying to  defend himself against Piccolo but  perhaps most impressively and what makes  me prefer this version of this set piece  more is how Goku uses it to manipulate  his opponent to create new Solutions  never before thought of when Goku is  faced with a hopeless situation he will  create a solution no one thought was  possible and he did so here not just  with his strength but with his strategy  and intelligence how you communicate to  your reader or viewer that your  character is strong that he's a powerful  individual not with big numbers or  Screaming but showing us first hand the  effort and misdirection he forces  Piccolo to work through it's an  impressive display placing Goku on a  pedestal alongside Piccolo at this  moment it truly truly feels as though  two demigods are duking it out with no  other living being even remotely coming  close demonstrating Innovations on  techniques I didn't even know I wanted  like firing the Kamehameha with his feet  allowing him to free up his hands for a  punch it's incredible the creativity on  display here and despite every thing  that's on the line time and again he's  forced to deny the help of anyone that  interferes now what a great and  impressive part of the story concerns  itself with Goku overcoming the odds and  managing to unleash more and more  ability and power his friends never  thought he had the other half of this  battle is supplied by Piccolo who in  turn shows his own brand of toughness  and grit to push through whether that be  the strength he demonstrates the  techniques he amazes us with or the  secret abilities of his race it seems  this character can create his own  alternative options when all others are  taken off the table and this tough  tenacious Dynamic Piccolo brings to the  table for Goku brings out the best in  his character both need this Victory so  much is hanging in the balance and  despite all of this Goku still refuses  to treat this like anything other than a  tournament and this moment this right  here this is where Goku stole Piccolo's  Soul it's in this moment Goku steam  Rising off of him and closed tattered  after taking the very best Piccolo has  to throw at him remains standing upright  before him smiling what an outrageously  brilliant fight after taking the  absolute best this Warrior has Goku  rallies himself one last time and with  fear in Piccolo's eyes the young man  Sprints towards the would-beat Demon  King Landing a devastating elbow to his  jaw it's honestly difficult not to just  sit back and commentate over all of this  fight the panels surrounding this  section of the manga are some of the  best in this series and even are some  toyotaro himself took inspiration for  his Dragon Ball super manga the poses  are just incredibly Dynamic the layouts  are incredible  the entire story of early Dragon Ball  has centered around a specific  philosophy to not train to win but to  better yourself and to protect those  that are defenseless in the 21st  Tenkaichi Budokai roshi desperately  wanted to instill this lesson in the  young Warrior and in doing so learned  that Goku was something truly special  even when he was a small boy he could  see that there was something outstanding  waiting to be tapped into even back then  it was apparent he wasn't like the  others pushing his master to his  absolute limits in the 22nd Tenkaichi  Budokai and Beyond Goku gained the  responsibility that such power brings  with it not because he wanted it but  because it was who he was and in the  face of that alongside a new generation  roshin hung up his ghee for good for the  first time in many many many years a  young boy was able to stand up when  others couldn't and save the world three  years pass now a young man Goku's limp  body lays defeated on the ground before  Piccolo who's now celebrating his  conquest of the earth and in no more  fitting a fashion as Kami rallies the  remaining Earth's Defenders to intervene  life surges back into Goku  this is what makes Goku special in the  face of certain death without any usable  Limbs and every option taken from him he  still finds it in him to dig deep smile  and invent a solution to the impossible  problems that stand before him no matter  how formidable no matter how terrifying  no matter the stakes no matter the odds  Goku will find a way to succeed when  others can't  foreign  [Applause]  sandwiched between two time skips  contains more passion skill vision and  love than many other arcs in this series  and indeed many other stories I've ever  read I started this video series in the  hopes that it would shed some light on  why I loved this story so much and I  hope I've managed to introduce at least  a few of you to what I consider to be  one of the most underrated stories to  have come out of Japan this was a much  needed enjoyable trip down memory lane  for me I haven't had the best year and a  half but this story definitely Has  Lifted my spirits in times when nothing  else could I thank you so much for  taking the time out of your days to  share it with me I don't know what the  future holds but I'm excited and I hope  I'll see you there  also like to thank TFS for contributing  to this video in the best of ways they  are some of the nicest most  accommodating individuals to work with  and you can find everything from their  personal twitters to their YouTube  channels Down Below in the description
 

